{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
  "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Viking River Cruises, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The outcome here is controlled by this Court's decisions in Concepcion, Epic, and Lamps Plus. After those decisions, a state is not free to simply declare that a state statute is too important to be relegated to bilateral arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Mr. Clement, if somebody else, a -- a different employee of Viking Cruises, brings a PAGA action that, by its terms, would include Ms. Moriana, would she be able to be included among the group of people, the large group of people, that would recover under that action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Viking River Cruises, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The provision -- and it's reproduced at page 13 of the blue brief --but it has essentially two subsections. The first involves the employee saying that they won't bring a class action, a collective action, or a private attorney general action, and then it continues to say that they won't participate as a member in a class action, a collective action, or a PAGA action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Give me a case in preemption law that says that a substantive state cause of action is implicitly preempted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the California Supreme Court in its Amalgamated decision and California in a recent brief have described PAGA as a procedural statute, not a substantive statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would we be bound by Erie by what the California courts think about this claim? Because it seems to me they've characterized it as procedural."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you have to say to his point that all that you've gotten rid of in PAGA actions are the things that were helpful or favorable to the defendant, you know, the adequate representation, the common questions of law or fact?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Nelson, can --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For purposes of the FAA question that is before us, are we bound by California's characterization of this PAGA claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nelson",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0003-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, instead, nine different violations on behalf of the entire sales force, California has made clear in the Williams case you get discovery coextensive with the class action. By the time we're done trying to figure that out in arbitration, we'd have to hire a claims administrator to give the checks and identify people. Nobody is going to do it. Arbitration will be gutted in practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1573",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b68b87cf1e61a20f7fc3a8ff02b4f1808ca4da26c4231206e5a54ebec01325",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b68b87cf1e-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:22 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
